From d4d351b55118de49f8ab6c204121e9f8dddbcd4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:50:18 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 142/144] render: a scenetexture set to a video file's path
 plays that video

A Wallpaper Engine preset can put a video of its own (`files/<name>.mp4`) where its base scene has an image slot, and
WE plays it there (Workshop preset 2843309472: a 194 MiB, 17-minute H.264 clip in its base 2388299037's
`newproperty` slot, whose project says `supportsvideo`). The core took only an image file's path (0139), so the
slot kept its texture.

RenderContext::resolveTexture now takes a name that is an absolute path ending in .mp4, .m4v, .webm, .mkv or .mov as
a video file: libavformat opens it and reads its video stream's coded size, and it becomes a video texture of that size
(TEXB0004, FIF_MP4, the file's path in Texture::videoFile) that GLPlayer streams from the file, as CVideo plays a
video wallpaper: silent, looped, on the scene's clock, like a video texture inside a scene. The file is never read
whole, so no byte cap applies (the preset's video is three times the image cap). A decoder holds several frames plus
references and hardware surfaces, so a video is capped below an image: 8192 px a side and 7680 x 4320 px (8K UHD,
GLPlayer::kFileMaxSide / kFileMaxPixels). A file that is missing, has no video stream or whose header is past a cap
throws AssetLoadException, which every caller reports and survives by keeping the slot's texture. The header is no
promise (a stream's size can change mid-way, a sample aspect stretches the output), so GLPlayer::setFrameCaps refuses
every frame over the caps as decoded or as displayed: the last good frame stays (blank before one), logged once.

A video texture also plays in any pass slot now: CPass counts every video texture its slots hold (other than its
image's own, which the scene already plays) as used for the pass's life and advances it each time the pass draws.
Before, only an image's own texture was ever started and updated, so a video in a usertexture slot, or a material's
video for a slot past its first, decoded its first frame at most and never drew it.

Tested by liascape's host_api_test usertexture_plays_a_video_file: kFourColoursMp4 as a file in the slot shows red at
0.1 s, blue at 0.6 s and red again at 1.1 s (looped); a missing .mp4 and a text file named .mp4 keep the slot's
texture; Matroska rawvideo files whose header says 8194 x 2 or 7682 x 4320 are refused with a health line naming the
cap, 8192 x 2 plays its grey; an MPEG-4 file 4096 x 16 with 4:1 samples (16384 wide as displayed) passes the header
and shows no frame (its grey without setFrameCaps). Without the CPass change the slot stayed the clear colour.

Origin: ours
Why: liascape docs/TODO.md #112 (a preset's video in a scene's texture slot plays)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Claude-Agent: claude-opus-5-5, effort high, preset video slots (#112)
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
